    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I hear you, but you're saying the concerns about judges being unqualified are just \"political talking points\" while the concerns about agency overreach are \"grounded in fundamental legal principle.\" Isn't it a bit of a stretch to dismiss the practical, real-world impact on regulatory expertise as just subjective politics? Can't you see how a legal framework that ignores technical expertise might be seen as inherently flawed by many legal scholars?",
